@layout()
  <div class="mb-6">
    <a href="/help" class="text-sm font-semibold text-sky-600 hover:text-sky-500">
      &larr; Back to Help
    </a>
  </div>

  <article class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-4">Create Illustrations</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-sm dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
      <p>
        Illustrations are the core content in SpeakerWindows. Each illustration represents a highlighted passage or quote you want to save and organize.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Creating a New Illustration</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
        <li>Click <strong>New Illustration</strong> from the illustrations page.</li>
        <li>Fill in the <strong>Title</strong> (required).</li>
        <li>Optionally add an <strong>Author</strong> and <strong>Source</strong>.</li>
        <li>Paste or type the content in the <strong>Content</strong> field.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Create</strong> to save.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Editing Illustrations</h2>
      <p>
        Open any illustration and click the <strong>Edit</strong> button to make changes. You can update the title, author, source, content, and tags at any time.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Tags</h2>
      <p>
        Tags help you organize and find illustrations later. When editing an illustration, you can add or remove tags to categorize your content.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
@end
